## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. God Controllers
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Fat controller with everything
public class OrderController : Controller {
    public async Task<IActionResult> CreateOrder(...) {
        // Validation
        // Database query
        // Email sending
        // Logging
        // Cache update
        // Inventory check
        // Payment processing
        // Return response
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Thin controller, delegate to services
public class OrderController : Controller {
    private readonly IOrderService _orderService;
    
    [HttpPost]
    public async Task<ActionResult<OrderDto>> CreateOrder(
        [FromBody] CreateOrderRequest request) {
        var order = await _orderService.CreateOrderAsync(request);
        return CreatedAtAction(nameof(GetOrder), new { id = order.Id }, order);
    }
}
```

### 2. Blocking Calls in Async Methods
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: .Result causes thread blocking
public async Task<Order> GetOrder(int id) {
    return _context.Orders.FirstOrDefaultAsync().Result; // BAD!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Proper async/await
public async Task<Order> GetOrder(int id) {
    return await _context.Orders.FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == id);
}
```

### 3. Disposing Scoped Services as Singleton
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: DbContext as Singleton
services.AddDbContext<DbContext>(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(connectionString));
services.AddSingleton<DbContext>(); // WRONG!

// ✅ GOOD: Proper registration
services.AddDbContext<DbContext>(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(connectionString));
// DbContext will be properly scoped
```

### 4. Missing Error Handling
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: No exception handling
[HttpGet("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<Product>> GetProduct(int id) {
    var product = await _context.Products.FindAsync(id);
    return Ok(product); // Throws if null!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Proper error handling
[HttpGet("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<Product>> GetProduct(int id) {
    var product = await _context.Products.FindAsync(id);
    if (product == null) {
        return NotFound();
    }
    return Ok(product);
}
```

### 5. No Request Validation
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: No validation
[HttpPost]
public async Task<IActionResult> CreateUser(CreateUserRequest request) {
    // request could be anything!
    var user = new User { Email = request.Email };
    await _context.Users.AddAsync(user);
}

// ✅ GOOD: Proper validation
[HttpPost]
public async Task<IActionResult> CreateUser(
    [FromBody, Required] CreateUserRequest request) {
    if (!ModelState.IsValid) {
        return BadRequest(ModelState);
    }
    
    var user = new User { Email = request.Email };
    await _context.Users.AddAsync(user);
}
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Use minimal APIs for simple endpoints**: Reduces ceremony
2. **Implement health checks**: Critical for container orchestration
3. **Use structured logging**: With correlation IDs
4. **Configure CORS properly**: Whitelist specific origins
5. **Use rate limiting**: Protect against abuse
6. **Implement API versioning**: For backward compatibility
7. **Use response compression**: gzip/brotli for performance
8. **Configure Kestrel properly**: For production workloads
9. **Use IOptions<T> pattern**: For strongly-typed configuration
10. **Implement global exception handling**: Consistent error responses

